# Federated traffic forecasting under a MEASURED V2X link — metr_la.npz

207 sensors partitioned into 4 RSU clients; 30 FedAvg rounds x 1 local epochs; horizon 12 steps. Link statistics are MEASURED from the official Eclipse MOSAIC ITS-G5 stack on the Dhaka R1 network (6,548,621 messages, delivery ratio 0.975).

| arm | MAE | vs centralized | uplink bytes | rounds | updates lost | link time s | wall s |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| centralized | 4.9755 | +0.0 % | 0.0 MB | 0 | 0 | 0 | 82.7 |
| local_only | 4.9895 | +0.3 % | 0.0 MB | 0 | 0 | 0 | 73.4 |
| federated | 4.9819 | +0.1 % | 1.8 MB | 30 | 0 | 0.0 | 130.0 |
| federated_v2x | 4.9795 | +0.1 % | 1.8 MB | 30 | 2 | 3.4 | 131.5 |

The accuracy column and the communication column come from the SAME experiment: this is the point where the forecasting chapters and the networking chapters meet.

Protocol: FedAvg (McMahan et al. 2017) over sensor-partitioned clients, following CNFGNN (Meng et al., KDD 2021) — with their analytic byte count replaced by a link whose loss and latency were measured in this project's own V2X simulation.

Partition assumption: sensors grouped into RSU coverage areas (spatial if coordinates exist, else contiguous blocks) — an assumption, not a surveyed deployment.

Regenerate: `python pipeline/forecasting/federated_forecast.py --data /home/ec2-user/in/metr_la.npz --clients 4 --rounds 30` (wall 417.5s).

The same command runs on any registered city — `pipeline/forecasting/city_datasets.py --list`.
